```
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import './App.css';

function TodoList() {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);
  const [newTodo, setNewTodo] = useState('');

  const handleSubmit = (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    setTodos([...todos, { text: newTodo, completed: false }]);
    setNewTodo('');
  };

  const handleDelete = (index) => {
    setTodos(todos.filter((todo, i) => i !== index));
  };

  const handleToggle = (index) => {
    setTodos(
      todos.map((todo, i) => {
        if (i === index) {
          return { ...todo, completed: !todo.completed };
        }
        return todo;
      })
    );
  };

  return (
    <div className="todo-list">
      <h1>Todo List</h1>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <input
          type="text"
          value={newTodo}
          onChange={(event) => setNewTodo(event.target.value)}
          placeholder="Enter new todo"
        />
        <button type="submit">Add Todo</button>
      </form>
      <ul>
        {todos.map((todo, index) => (
          <li key={index}>
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={todo.completed}
              onClick={() => handleToggle(index)}
            />
            <span style={{ textDecoration: todo.completed ? 'line-through' : 'none' }}>
              {todo.text}
            </span>
            <button onClick={() => handleDelete(index)}>X</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

export default TodoList;
```
This code creates a todo list with the following features:

* A text input field to add new todos
* A submit button to add new todos
* A list of existing todos, with each todo displaying the text, a checkbox to mark it as completed, and a delete button
* The ability to delete a todo
* The ability to toggle the completion of a todo

The code uses the `useState` hook to manage the state of the todos and the new todo input field. The `handleSubmit` function is called when the submit button is clicked, and it adds a new todo to the list and resets the input field. The `handleDelete` function is called when a delete button is clicked, and it removes the corresponding todo from the list. The `handleToggle` function is called when a checkbox is clicked, and it toggles the completion of the corresponding todo.

